response:
According to Article 4(11) of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), the factors that may reveal that the data controller projects offering goods or services to interested parties in the Union are:

* The data controller is offering goods or services remotely to interested parties in the Union;
* The data controller is addressing to the public in a Member State;
* The data controller has specified its offering in a language commonly used in one of the Member States;
* The data controller has a legal representative or a nominated representative in one of the Member States;
* The data controller has referred to the internal data protection legislation of the Union;
* The data controller has indicated that it is in the data subject's interest to use such goods or services.

These factors can indicate that the data controller is targeting individuals in the Union and, therefore, is required to comply with the GDPR.
